# Node backend

Runtime is Node 22 (`engines` in `functions/package.json`). Root `package.json` scripts delegate into `functions`.

## Process model

- `functions/src/index.ts` — Cloud Function `api`. Bootstraps once, then forwards to Express. No WebSocket on this export.
- `functions/src/server.ts` — local and long-running host. Calls `setupLiveInterviewWebSocket` and `setupV2LiveInterviewWebSocket` after `listen`.
- `functions/src/app.ts` — helmet, CORS, Firestore config refresh, `express.json`, rate limits, routes. On the Cloud Function the prefix is empty because the function name is `api`. Locally the prefix is `/api` (`isCloudRuntime()`).

## Route pattern

```typescript
router.post(
  '/start',
  validate(startBodySchema),
  asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
    const result = await interviewService.startInterview(req.user!.uid, req.body);
    sendCreated(res, result, 'Interview started');
  }),
);
```

- Validate with Zod via `functions/src/middleware/validation.middleware.ts`.
- Wrap with `asyncHandler`. Throw `AppError` for expected failures.
- Respond with `sendSuccess` / `sendCreated` from `functions/src/shared/responses`. Envelope is `{ success, message, data }`.
- Authenticated v2 routes sit behind `verifyToken` in `v2.routes.ts`. Public exceptions already mounted above it: subscription plans and Razorpay webhook, `interview-invites`, `invites`.
- New interview routes belong on `functions/src/modules/v2/interview.routes.ts`, mounted at `/v2/interviews`.

## Services

- Interview lifecycle: `functions/src/services/interview.service.ts`.
- Gemini: `functions/src/library/gemini-client.ts` only. Model names come from Firestore `config/genai` or env (`getDefaultModel`, `getDefaultLiveModel`).
- Logging: `functions/src/shared/logger`. Do not log tokens or raw audio.

## Commands

- Dev server: `npm run dev` from this repo (default port 5000; the frontend local base is `http://localhost:5000/api`).
- Compile: `npm run build`.
- Unit test: `npm test` inside `functions` (`ai-turn.test.ts` only).

Do not deploy (`deploy-functions`, `deploy-websocket`, indexes, storage) unless the task asks for a deploy.
